<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 4 Best in Slot Gear list for Holy Paladin Healer in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Icecrown Citadel. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Holy Paladin Healer Phase 4</h2>
<i>Healer gearing always heavily depends on playstyle, situation and raid environment so treat the BiS list below as a guideline rather than a gospel.</i>
<br/>
<br/>Due to being able to wear all 4 armor types, Holy Paladin gearing can be somewhat overwhelming as it has a ton of options. With a little bit of work and stat evaluations, we can cut this down tremendously and also consider loot priority carefully, as mail and plate spellpower gear is very uncontested in return.<br/>
<br/>You can finally shed your T8 set bonus in ICC, as the raw ilvl of gear is high enough to make up for the healing difference. Additionally, the T10 2pc set bonus <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70755/item-paladin-t10-holy-2p-bonus">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Item - Paladin T10 Holy 2P Bonus</span></a> is very strong and makes your already impressive cooldown list even stronger. The best part is, unlike previous phases, you won't really have major competition with tiersets as you can purchase the 251 tier outright with only emblems, and upgrading to 264 only takes fairly easy to acquire tokens. 277 tier will definitely be much harder to acquire, but you'll only need two pieces compared to most peoples' four.<br/>
<br/>We will only be using 2 pieces of tier, as most of it is poorly itemized compared to offpieces and the 4pc is fairly weak. This reduces the amount of emblems you'll be needing tremendously, compared to other classes.<br/>
<br/>The sets have been divided into "realistic" and "absolute" BiS as in previous phases, and absolute will generally be fairly difficult to acquire as it requires farming multiple difficult 25H bosses. The realistic set downgrades some of the hardest or most contested 25H options to 10H or in some cases changes a hard 25H boss to an easier one to put on farm - but in general, remember that "realistic" is a subjective measure. How contested an item is is highly dependent on your raid group and loot system, and most importantly RNG on whether an item drops (or drops very often!)<br/>
