<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="rings">Rings for Holy Paladin Healer Phase 4</h3>Icecrown Citadel brings a unique reputation-based raid reward in the form of the Ashen Verdict ring, which "levels up" from ilvl 251 to 277 as you increase rep with <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/faction=1156/the-ashen-verdict">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Ashen Verdict</span></a>. The Revered and Exalted versions of the healer ring have a random spellpower proc, which isn't really great, but they're still "free" rings, so we'll take it.<br/>
<br/>Since the rep rings effectively mean everyone in your raid only needs one ring slot filled with drops, this slot is a lot less stressful to fill than before. However, a curious perk with the rings is that all of the versions below Exalted are kind of bad - the Revered one in particular doesn't gain any stats from the Honored version, and then it gets a MASSIVE budget boost at Exalted where it's a 277 stat budget + the proc for free. <br/>
<br/>Overall, this means <b>consider equipping the Ashen Verdict ring only after you get the Exalted version, and don't equip the Friendly or Honored ones unless you have no other options</b>; regular 264 rings are statted much better than even the 268 version by a lot, since it lacks a socket and the proc isn't very good for us.<br/>
<br/>The top two non-AV rings are interchangeable; just pick between mp5 or crit. However, the haste/<wbr/>crit one will obviously be a lot more contested than the mp5 ring, which is essentially healers-only. <br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Ring Enchant</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=44636/enchant-ring-greater-spellpower">
