<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="weapons">Weapons and Offhands for Holy Paladin Healer Phase 4</h2>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="main-hand-weapons-for-holy-paladin-healer-phase-4">Main Hand Weapons for Holy Paladin Healer Phase 4</h4>
<a class="q5 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46017/valanyr-hammer-of-ancient-kings">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_99.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Val'anyr, Hammer of Ancient Kings</span></a> continues to be BiS and will remain so for the rest of the expansion, since in WotLK Classic it was buffed to 258 ilvl.<br/>
<br/>If you're in the situation where you don't have one, then your options become somewhat interesting. While traditionally thought of as a raid healer weapon, Glyph of Holy Light interacts with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50685/trauma">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_118.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Trauma</span></a>, so it can actually be somewhat good on fights like Sindragosa. The proc is very feast or famine though, very dependent on fight damage profiles; with constant aoe, it's pretty good, while without that it's mediocre at best with the lost secondary stats.<br/>
<br/>However, even with it having a bit of variance, the proc is just good enough to where it really only contends with 25H Lich King weapons - which the vast vast majority of people won't have access to. In other words, use Trauma if you don't have Val'anyr, it's pretty ok!<br/>
<br/>Since there are a ton of weapon options available and most are duplicates of each other (the 25 LK swords and maces have identical stats for example), this list will be fairly trimmed down. Just remember that most of the stat budget in weapons is in the spellpower, and at the massive amounts that weapons have, it actually matters even for Holy Paladin, so just pick the highest ilvl weapons you have access to (or Trauma) and you'll be fine.<br/>
<br/>
